OL,3,GNEWSA'My children think I've lost my
OL,4,Amind': The Scot prepping for when the
OL,5,Alights go out
OL,6,
OL,7,FInside Brian's home is enough food to
OL,8,Ffeed his family for 165 days.
OL,10,FHe's also storing hundreds of gallons
OL,11,Fof fresh water, two generators, battery
OL,12,Fpower packs and stacks of military
OL,13,Frations.
OL,15,FThe 52-year-old lift engineer, who
OL,16,Flives in Croy near Cumbernauld, says he
OL,17,Fhas spent about #2,500 on freeze-dried
OL,18,Ffood alone this year.
OL,20,F"My children think I've lost my mind,"
OL,21,Fhe says.
OL,23,APub: 20-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
